WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.577
A RAG system must have a plan for document updates.

00:00:03.577 --> 00:00:09.177
Imagine that a policy changes but the old chunks remain in the vector database.

00:00:09.177 --> 00:00:15.992
Retrieval may continue returning outdated evidence even though the language model is working perfectly.

00:00:15.992 --> 00:00:23.967
A practical update workflow detects changed documents, removes or marks the old chunks, creates new chunks,

00:00:23.967 --> 00:00:28.367
generates new embeddings, and upserts the new records.

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:32.412
Then the evaluation questions should be run again.

00:00:32.412 --> 00:00:37.457
Keep version information and updated dates in metadata whenever possible.

00:00:37.457 --> 00:00:44.797
Freshness is especially important for policies, product documentation, pricing, regulations,

00:00:44.797 --> 00:00:51.207
and internal procedures. Indexing is not a one-time activity in a living system.

00:00:51.207 --> 00:00:57.622
Production RAG needs a repeatable ingestion and re-indexing process so the knowledge base stays aligned with

00:00:57.622 --> 00:00:59.862
the underlying sources.
